<description>&lt;p&gt;Coordinated cattle raids in Warrup state killed at least 72 people, while a drone strike on a market in Abyei killed at least 73, intensifying violence in South Sudan. President Kiir reshuffled the South Sudan Revenue Authority board, reinstating two commissioners after a cancelled order, and the Bar Association launched a roadmap to improve access to justice. The government partnered with Israel's Gilat to provide nationwide satellite internet and secured a UNESCO world-heritage nomination for the Boma-Bandingilo inscription. Governor Dollar promoted the reintegration of IDPs and returnees, and the U.S. Embassy remembered staff who died supporting South Sudanese people. 2 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxPS2hOV1BldlVpaGRtdk1IdjA5VGxNQS10a0NPcWEzczV1aHRfXzFtX3I0UHRoWXVZTHBNaEZDMzhpQ0lCYVFybFJZeGRlU09DQmtHS0dzWm9ROFNNYUZRQXFjWldhZEFsenFyX09MSmJMR3dFOC1WUUM2SkJCZHNEZk1TSFMtMzc0ZngweG9WVFh0a0FSSy1JeVZFdjJoUF9iV2haT0wzamNNNlpSdjBLVFp1ZkdGQ1lXXzAzNmROSk81QQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;ohchr&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTFA2a1d1OTh2TGlzOWlTODRaLXBTSkxLcXRmb1BMVzByM2VwZDFWc3BVWFEtSi1CWWRNOU5OZTlFbmFxNWoyblVwS1BLaUpwbTBHOFZkaEg1eXlXaFU3TnpPb2FPQURJUHFTQzlsc0dzVGQ3Vk9OVTh2NHpPSG9sd0E?oc=5&quot;&gt;FRCN HQ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxOZ2JWa0JmV3VQQUIxM3lFdFJGYWVBbi1nRDVxQ01hTmNISEFjeTF5UXVTYTY4UnFVRUgweHZqX2VlZGUwYlRNZ3l5Z0o2OGZXQVNSYmtpQWZBVXdTS0lIVzFtZ2JKMFBwY0ViM2xvaThOVjRmNURMSE0wdkoyNGY5bjh6UTB3VWplRU50ZmVkbTBqWUxTVGc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Uzalendo News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxPX24xZm11ZEpkMlA1WTFyeXlfOXpsY1Mw